{
  "about": "A project's activation through a scripted host-functions port, by host (#3778 group 2): the lock verification, the bindings and the cases of each called function, which the case's functions member scripts as project_functions.json's do. Moved at 8e662c648 from the doubles of declaration_project_files.rs, file_project.rs and project_diagnostics.rs. The project of the first two lists one function file with a callable for each host, a lock for each host and a codelist file, beside the specification's entry directory; file_project.rs's study differed only in the function file's directory and the R lock, which its cases do not read, and its unlocked cases remove the environments and both locks. project_diagnostics.rs's project lists two integer identities with the Python lock, and its single-function cases list an integer identity or a text function instead. Each case reports through the file route, which names each file by its path in the study, reports a function file's finding in that file with the project as its entry and its listing as its environment path, and refuses an unclassified host failure as engine_rejected opaque_host at step build. The calls each port received are in function_call_contracts.json.",
  "documents": {
    "project": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: project\nfunctions: [functions/id.yaml]\nenvironments:\n  python: {lock: uv.lock}\n  r: {lock: renv.lock}\ncodelists: [ct.yaml]\n",
    "id": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: function\nname: id\ndescription: Integer identity.\nparams: [{name: x, type: int, accepts_missing: true}]\nreturns: int\nmay_return_missing: true\nimplementations: {python: program.id, r: program::id}\ntests:\n  - {id: normal, covers: [normal, boundary], args: {x: 7}, result: 7}\n  - {id: missing, covers: ['accepted-missing:x', nullable-output], args: {x: null}, result: null}\n",
    "uv.lock": "version = 1\npackage = []\n",
    "renv.lock": "{\"R\": {\"Version\": \"4.6.1\"}, \"Packages\": {}}\n",
    "codelists": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: codelists\ncodelists: [{id: SEX, name: Sex, items: [{value: F}, {value: M}]}]\n",
    "domain": "yamaa: '1.0'\ntype: spec\ndomain: TEST\ninput: {SRC: {path: input.csv, types: {ID: int}}}\nkeys: [ID]\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: int, derivation: SRC.ID}\n  - {name: VALUE, type: int, derivation: {function: {name: id, args: {x: SRC.ID}}}}\noutput: {path: output.csv, columns: [ID, VALUE]}\n",
    "identities": "yamaa: '1.0'\ntype: project\nfunctions: [functions/first.yaml, functions/second.yaml]\nenvironments: {python: {lock: uv.lock}}\n",
    "first": "yamaa: '1.0'\ntype: function\nname: first\ndescription: Integer identity.\nparams: [{name: x, type: int}]\nreturns: int\nimplementations: {python: project.first}\ntests:\n  - {id: normal, covers: [normal], args: {x: 7}, result: 7}\n  - {id: boundary, covers: [boundary], args: {x: -9223372036854775808}, result: -9223372036854775808}\n  - {id: missing, covers: ['short-circuit-missing:x'], args: {x: null}, result: null}\n",
    "both": "yamaa: '1.0'\ntype: spec\ndomain: TEST\ninput: {SRC: {path: input.csv, types: {ID: int}}}\nkeys: [ID]\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: int, derivation: SRC.ID}\n  - {name: FIRST, type: int, derivation: {function: {name: first, args: {x: SRC.ID}}}}\n  - {name: SECOND, type: int, derivation: {function: {name: second, args: {x: SRC.ID}}}}\noutput: {path: output.csv, columns: [ID, FIRST, SECOND]}\n",
    "text": "yamaa: '1.0'\ntype: function\nname: text\ndescription: Text\nparams: []\nreturns: str\nimplementations: {python: project.text}\ntests: [{id: text, covers: [normal, boundary], args: {}, result: \"authored \\u00e9\\0\\U0001F642\"}]\n"
  },
